2.Why FaultContract is required in WCF?
ans:
    By default WCF does not allow parsing of exceptions from service to client. In order to pass any fault, we have to define fault contract 
as a type of contract that can be parsed to client. The same way we can throw FaultExceprion instance , so that client can read the excception details.

    Fault contract gives the option to customise error message, instead of parsing it direct exception.
